        ["What does ACSM recommend for the duration of a static stretch hold for most adults?",["About 10-30 seconds","About 1-3 seconds","About 2-3 minutes","About 5 minutes"],"Holding a static stretch about 10-30 seconds is recommended for most adults, adding up to about 60 seconds per muscle group. Older adults may benefit from 30-60 second holds."],
        ["A sedentary 70-year-old is starting resistance training. Which starting intensity is most appropriate?",["About 40-50% of 1RM with 10-15 reps","About 90% of 1RM for 3 reps","Maximal effort for 1 rep each set","Bodyweight only with no plan to progress"],"ACSM suggests that beginners and older adults can start with light loads of about 40-50% 1RM to build tolerance safely. The program should still progress over time."],
        ["Two clients follow the same program; one improves much faster. Which principle explains this?",["Individuality","Reversibility","Specificity","Overload"],"People differ in genetics, training history, sleep, and stress, so they respond differently to the same program. Programs should be adjusted to each person."],
        ["A patient performs 3 sets of 10 squats with 20 kg. What is the training volume for this exercise?",["600 kg","60 kg","200 kg","33 kg"],"Volume load = sets x reps x load = 3 x 10 x 20 = 600 kg. Answering 200 kg leaves out the number of sets."],
        ["At the end of a set, a patient says they could have done about 2 more reps with good form. What does this describe?",["Two repetitions in reserve","A one-repetition maximum effort","Muscular failure on the final rep","An RPE of 20 on the Borg scale"],"Repetitions in reserve is the number of additional reps possible at the end of a set. Two in reserve means the set stopped short of failure."],
        ["A patient's program calls for 3 x 8-12. On two consecutive sessions, she completes 14 reps in her last set with good form. What is the BEST next step?",["Increase the load slightly at the next session","Keep the load the same for another month","Decrease the load and add a fourth set","Switch to a different exercise for that muscle"],"Exceeding the target range by two or more reps on two consecutive sessions signals readiness for a small load increase (the 2-for-2 rule)."],
        ["A planned week of reduced training load inserted after several hard weeks is called what?",["A deload","A macrocycle","Detraining","Specificity"],"A deload deliberately lowers load to allow recovery while keeping the habit of training. Detraining is an unplanned loss of adaptation from stopping."],
        ["A firefighter must carry heavy equipment up stairs. Which program BEST applies the SAID principle?",["Loaded stair climbs and weighted carries","Seated machine curls at light loads","Long slow cycling at a low intensity","Static stretching of all major muscles"],"SAID calls for training that matches the demand: loaded, upright, multi-joint work under fatigue. The other options build qualities that transfer poorly to the task."]
